phantomos-config — SKELETON, ships no configuration yet
=====================================================

This package exists so that the package set installed in an image matches the
inventory in the spec. The inventory names phantomos-config in the base set; if this
package did not exist, the M1 inventory diff would have to be corrected for a package
that is simply not built yet, which is the kind of exception that outlives its reason.

Content lands in M2, per the spec's §4.3: Xfconf and gsettings defaults, the dotfile
skeleton, sysctl, AppArmor local profiles, systemd user-unit drop-ins, nftables rules,
the Firefox enterprise policies (§6.9) and the live-console autologin decision (§12
item 10). The install rule from §4.3 applies then: postinst writes only files that are
absent, never overwrites a user's edit.

To check whether you are looking at the real thing:
  dpkg -L phantomos-config
Until M2 that list contains this file and nothing else.
